# Soma's screen record tile (123+). Calibrated on the Mac's Fold8 emulator (Android 17), 2026-10-22: click-tile answers
# only with Quick Settings open, and Android 17 asks "Share one app" -> "Share entire screen" -> "Share screen".
# A clean start: no shade or dialog left by an earlier walk.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
key BACK
key HOME
shell cmd statusbar expand-settings
wait 1000
shell cmd statusbar click-tile dev.omalauncher.boss/dev.omalauncher.record.ScreenRecordTile
wait 2500
expect Share your screen
shot capture-prompt
# Since 132 the prompt opens on the entire screen (it asked for one app before).
expect Share entire screen
absent Share one app
tap Share screen
wait 4500
shot recording
# While it records, the shade holds the time and Stop (the Mac's look at the b27919abe walk).
shell cmd statusbar expand-notifications
wait 1200
# Android hides private notifications' content while the screen is recorded: this one is public (137 walk: only a bare header showed).
expect Recording · tap to stop
expect Stop
shot recording-in-shade
shell cmd statusbar collapse
wait 800
shell cmd statusbar expand-settings
wait 1000
shell cmd statusbar click-tile dev.omalauncher.boss/dev.omalauncher.record.ScreenRecordTile
wait 2000
shell cmd statusbar expand-notifications
expect Screen recording saved
shot saved-notice
shell cmd statusbar collapse
[phone] Add Screen record to Samsung's Quick Settings; tap it, allow, record a few seconds, tap the tile again; the saved notice opens the video in Movies/Soma.
[phone] Start a recording, lock the phone, unlock it, stop: say whether the lock screen shows in the video.
[phone] Tap the Screen record tile: Android's prompt asks for the entire screen (no "A single app" choice), and the video is of the whole screen.
[phone] After Share screen: a big 3, 2, 1 in the middle, gone before recording; a short buzz as it starts; nothing of ours on screen while it records; the shade's notification shows the time and Stop, and Stop (or a tap on it) ends it with "Screen recording saved" (Boss, 2026-10-22).
